      "id": 1,
      "text": "Troutman’s roots trace back to the 1750s when Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Maryland immigrants claimed free land in North Carolina’s Piedmont.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.troutmannc.gov/166/History-of-Community"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Jacob Troutman secured 200 acres at Norrids Creek in 1778, cementing the family name in local history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.troutmannc.gov/166/History-of-Community"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Atlantic, Tennessee and Ohio Railroad opened in 1858, establishing Troutman Depot and putting the town on the regional map.",
